Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:44:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 28/29] volume: apply fsGroup ownership on FreeBSD

SetVolumeOwnership was built for Linux only; elsewhere NewVolumeOwnership
returned a no-op, so on FreeBSD no volume (secret, configMap, projected,
emptyDir, PV) was given the pod's fsGroup: a non-root container got
EACCES on a secret with defaultMode 0440 although fsGroup was among its
groups. The Linux implementation only uses POSIX calls; build it for
FreeBSD too (renamed volume_linux.go to volume_ownership_unix.go, since
the _linux suffix restricts a file to Linux whatever its build tags).
Its tests pass on FreeBSD.
---
 pkg/volume/{volume_linux.go => volume_ownership_unix.go}        | 2 +-
 .../{volume_linux_test.go => volume_ownership_unix_test.go}     | 2 +-
 pkg/volume/volume_unsupported.go                                | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 rename pkg/volume/{volume_linux.go => volume_ownership_unix.go} (99%)
 rename pkg/volume/{volume_linux_test.go => volume_ownership_unix_test.go} (99%)

diff --git a/pkg/volume/volume_linux.go b/pkg/volume/volume_ownership_unix.go
similarity index 99%
rename from pkg/volume/volume_linux.go
rename to pkg/volume/volume_ownership_unix.go
index 48e6a8f385e..10c55b5cf24 100644
--- a/pkg/volume/volume_linux.go
+++ b/pkg/volume/volume_ownership_unix.go
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-//go:build linux
+//go:build linux || freebsd
 
